  24:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****   @verbatim
  25:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****   ==============================================================================
  26:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****                         ##### How to use this driver #####
  27:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****   ==============================================================================
  28:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****   [..]
  29:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****     This driver implements a high level communication layer for read and write from/to
  30:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****     this memory. The needed STM32 hardware resources (SDMMC and GPIO) are performed by
  31:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****     the user in HAL_MMC_MspInit() function (MSP layer).
ARM GAS  C:\Users\OUFARU~1\AppData\Local\Temp\ccIuOg5Q.s 			page 2


  32:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****     Basically, the MSP layer configuration should be the same as we provide in the
  33:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****     examples.
  34:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****     You can easily tailor this configuration according to hardware resources.
  35:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c **** 
  36:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****   [..]
  37:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****     This driver is a generic layered driver for SDMMC memories which uses the HAL
  38:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****     SDMMC driver functions to interface with MMC and eMMC cards devices.
  39:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****     It is used as follows:
  40:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c **** 
  41:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****     (#)Initialize the SDMMC low level resources by implement the HAL_MMC_MspInit() API:
  42:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****         (##) Enable the SDMMC interface clock using __HAL_RCC_SDMMC_CLK_ENABLE();
  43:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****         (##) SDMMC pins configuration for MMC card
  44:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****             (+++) Enable the clock for the SDMMC GPIOs using the functions __HAL_RCC_GPIOx_CLK_ENAB
  45:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****             (+++) Configure these SDMMC pins as alternate function pull-up using HAL_GPIO_Init()
  46:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****                   and according to your pin assignment;
  47:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****         (##) NVIC configuration if you need to use interrupt process (HAL_MMC_ReadBlocks_IT()
  48:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****              and HAL_MMC_WriteBlocks_IT() APIs).
  49:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****             (+++) Configure the SDMMC interrupt priorities using function HAL_NVIC_SetPriority();
  50:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****             (+++) Enable the NVIC SDMMC IRQs using function HAL_NVIC_EnableIRQ()
  51:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****             (+++) SDMMC interrupts are managed using the macros __HAL_MMC_ENABLE_IT()
  52:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****                   and __HAL_MMC_DISABLE_IT() inside the communication process.
  53:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****             (+++) SDMMC interrupts pending bits are managed using the macros __HAL_MMC_GET_IT()
  54:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****                   and __HAL_MMC_CLEAR_IT()
  55:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****         (##) No general propose DMA Configuration is needed, an Internal DMA for SDMMC Peripheral a
  56:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c **** 
  57:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****     (#) At this stage, you can perform MMC read/write/erase operations after MMC card initializatio
  58:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c **** 
  59:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****   *** MMC Card Initialization and configuration ***
  60:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****   ================================================
  61:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****   [..]
  62:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****     To initialize the MMC Card, use the HAL_MMC_Init() function. It Initializes
  63:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****     SDMMC Peripheral (STM32 side) and the MMC Card, and put it into StandBy State (Ready for data t
  64:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****     This function provide the following operations:
  65:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c **** 
  66:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****     (#) Initialize the SDMMC peripheral interface with default configuration.
  67:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****         The initialization process is done at 400KHz. You can change or adapt
  68:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****         this frequency by adjusting the "ClockDiv" field.
  69:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****         The MMC Card frequency (SDMMC_CK) is computed as follows:
  70:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c **** 
  71:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****            SDMMC_CK = SDMMCCLK / (2 * ClockDiv)
  72:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c **** 
  73:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****         In initialization mode and according to the MMC Card standard,
  74:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****         make sure that the SDMMC_CK frequency doesn't exceed 400KHz.
  75:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c **** 
  76:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****         This phase of initialization is done through SDMMC_Init() and
  77:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****         SDMMC_PowerState_ON() SDMMC low level APIs.
  78:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c **** 
  79:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****     (#) Initialize the MMC card. The API used is HAL_MMC_InitCard().
  80:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****         This phase allows the card initialization and identification
  81:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****         and check the MMC Card type (Standard Capacity or High Capacity)
  82:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****         The initialization flow is compatible with MMC standard.
  83:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c **** 
  84:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****         This API (HAL_MMC_InitCard()) could be used also to reinitialize the card in case
  85:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****         of plug-off plug-in.
  86:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c **** 
  87:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****     (#) Configure the MMC Card Data transfer frequency. By Default, the card transfer
  88:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****         frequency by adjusting the "ClockDiv" field.
ARM GAS  C:\Users\OUFARU~1\AppData\Local\Temp\ccIuOg5Q.s 			page 3


  89:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****         In transfer mode and according to the MMC Card standard, make sure that the
  90:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****         SDMMC_CK frequency doesn't exceed 25MHz and 100MHz in High-speed mode switch.
  91:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c **** 
  92:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****     (#) Select the corresponding MMC Card according to the address read with the step 2.
  93:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c **** 
  94:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****     (#) Configure the MMC Card in wide bus mode: 4-bits data.
  95:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****     (#) Select the MMC Card partition using HAL_MMC_SwitchPartition()
  96:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c **** 
  97:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****   *** MMC Card Read operation ***
  98:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****   ==============================
  99:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****   [..]
 100:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****     (+) You can read from MMC card in polling mode by using function HAL_MMC_ReadBlocks().
 101:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****         This function support only 512-bytes block length (the block size should be
 102:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****         chosen as 512 bytes).
 103:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****         You can choose either one block read operation or multiple block read operation
 104:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****         by adjusting the "NumberOfBlocks" parameter.
 105:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****         After this, you have to ensure that the transfer is done correctly. The check is done
 106:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****         through HAL_MMC_GetCardState() function for MMC card state.
 107:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c **** 
 108:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****     (+) You can read from MMC card in DMA mode by using function HAL_MMC_ReadBlocks_DMA().
 109:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****         This function support only 512-bytes block length (the block size should be
 110:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****         chosen as 512 bytes).
 111:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****         You can choose either one block read operation or multiple block read operation
 112:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****         by adjusting the "NumberOfBlocks" parameter.
 113:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****         After this, you have to ensure that the transfer is done correctly. The check is done
 114:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****         through HAL_MMC_GetCardState() function for MMC card state.
 115:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****         You could also check the DMA transfer process through the MMC Rx interrupt event.
 116:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c **** 
 117:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****     (+) You can read from MMC card in Interrupt mode by using function HAL_MMC_ReadBlocks_IT().
 118:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****         This function allows the read of 512 bytes blocks.
 119:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****         You can choose either one block read operation or multiple block read operation
 120:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****         by adjusting the "NumberOfBlocks" parameter.
 121:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****         After this, you have to ensure that the transfer is done correctly. The check is done
 122:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****         through HAL_MMC_GetCardState() function for MMC card state.
 123:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****         You could also check the IT transfer process through the MMC Rx interrupt event.
