 260:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****       (+) MspDeInitCallback  : MMC MspDeInit.
 261:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****     This function takes as parameters the HAL peripheral handle, the Callback ID
 262:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****     and a pointer to the user callback function.
 263:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c **** 
 264:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****     Use function HAL_MMC_UnRegisterCallback() to reset a callback to the default
 265:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****     weak (overridden) function. It allows to reset following callbacks:
 266:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****       (+) TxCpltCallback : callback when a transmission transfer is completed.
 267:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****       (+) RxCpltCallback : callback when a reception transfer is completed.
 268:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****       (+) ErrorCallback : callback when error occurs.
 269:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****       (+) AbortCpltCallback : callback when abort is completed.
 270:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****       (+) Read_DMADblBuf0CpltCallback : callback when the DMA reception of first buffer is complete
 271:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****       (+) Read_DMADblBuf1CpltCallback : callback when the DMA reception of second buffer is complet
 272:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****       (+) Write_DMADblBuf0CpltCallback : callback when the DMA transmission of first buffer is comp
 273:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****       (+) Write_DMADblBuf1CpltCallback : callback when the DMA transmission of second buffer is com
 274:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****       (+) MspInitCallback    : MMC MspInit.
 275:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****       (+) MspDeInitCallback  : MMC MspDeInit.
 276:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****     This function) takes as parameters the HAL peripheral handle and the Callback ID.
 277:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c **** 
 278:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****     By default, after the HAL_MMC_Init and if the state is HAL_MMC_STATE_RESET
 279:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****     all callbacks are reset to the corresponding legacy weak (overridden) functions.
 280:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****     Exception done for MspInit and MspDeInit callbacks that are respectively
 281:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****     reset to the legacy weak (overridden) functions in the HAL_MMC_Init
 282:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****     and HAL_MMC_DeInit only when these callbacks are null (not registered beforehand).
 283:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****     If not, MspInit or MspDeInit are not null, the HAL_MMC_Init and HAL_MMC_DeInit
 284:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****     keep and use the user MspInit/MspDeInit callbacks (registered beforehand)
 285:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c **** 
 286:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****     Callbacks can be registered/unregistered in READY state only.
 287:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****     Exception done for MspInit/MspDeInit callbacks that can be registered/unregistered
 288:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****     in READY or RESET state, thus registered (user) MspInit/DeInit callbacks can be used
 289:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****     during the Init/DeInit.
 290:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****     In that case first register the MspInit/MspDeInit user callbacks
 291:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****     using HAL_MMC_RegisterCallback before calling HAL_MMC_DeInit
 292:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****     or HAL_MMC_Init function.
 293:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c **** 
 294:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****     When The compilation define USE_HAL_MMC_REGISTER_CALLBACKS is set to 0 or
 295:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****     not defined, the callback registering feature is not available
 296:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****     and weak (overridden) callbacks are used.
 297:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c **** 
 298:Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_mmc.c ****   @endverbatim
